WEBVTT

00:01.330 --> 00:08.290
<i>Can you imagine a life where you 
can't even touch the person you love?</i>

00:09.160 --> 00:14.130
<i>The curse the witch laid upon him caused 
him to take the lives of any he touched.</i>

00:14.780 --> 00:19.110
<i>His own mother distanced herself from him,
 his friends called him a monster...</i>

00:19.110 --> 00:20.500
<i>Even people he'd never met spoke of him as</i>

00:20.500 --> 00:23.490
<i>"death incarnate that dwells in the forest."</i>

00:24.140 --> 00:29.210
<i>And yet, he doesn't feel 
the least bit lonely.</i>

00:30.390 --> 00:32.280
Wow, a string telephone!

00:32.280 --> 00:33.720
I remember these!

00:34.590 --> 00:37.130
We used to play with these all 
the time when we were kids!

00:37.130 --> 00:42.000
With this, I can speak to you 
even when I'm in the next room.

00:44.800 --> 00:46.730
I'll give it a try.

00:49.440 --> 00:52.250
For my first time with Your Grace, I'll...

01:01.070 --> 01:03.280
Did you hear what I said?

01:03.280 --> 01:05.980
I can't say it with my own lips.

01:06.300 --> 01:07.560
Then it worked!

02:38.010 --> 02:42.070
Episode 19
The Duke, Alice, and the Encounter in the Witches' World

02:42.400 --> 02:43.970
Huh? What is this place?

02:44.650 --> 02:46.930
You're dressed in a cute outfit...

02:46.930 --> 02:48.440
And so am I?

02:48.810 --> 02:53.650
It appears we've been sucked 
into another book I was reading.

02:53.650 --> 02:56.610
Oh, this happened before.

02:57.260 --> 03:00.270
Last time it was Wonderland, so...

03:01.610 --> 03:04.580
Is this "Little Red Riding Hood"?

03:05.160 --> 03:06.290
Indeed!

03:06.740 --> 03:09.540
I'm Little Red Riding Hood!

03:09.840 --> 03:10.780
It's really her!

03:10.780 --> 03:11.860
I want an autograph!

03:11.860 --> 03:12.750
Quiet.

03:12.970 --> 03:16.260
There's a naughty wolf in the house up ahead.

03:16.260 --> 03:17.710
I want you to defeat it for me!

03:18.260 --> 03:19.680
A wolf?

03:19.680 --> 03:21.130
If you can defeat it,

03:21.130 --> 03:23.220
I'll grant you any wish!

03:23.490 --> 03:24.540
Really?

03:24.540 --> 03:26.100
Can you break my curse?

03:26.100 --> 03:28.310
Of course! Leave it to me!

03:29.830 --> 03:33.770
By the way, why am I dressed like a wolf?

03:34.070 --> 03:37.340
So he'll think you're a buddy 
and let his guard down, duh!

03:37.340 --> 03:38.950
Now go!

03:38.950 --> 03:39.740
Go!

03:40.390 --> 03:44.170
She's scary! She's got 
a nasty sadistic streak!

03:44.170 --> 03:45.200
There, there.

03:48.380 --> 03:52.320
Alice, when are you going 
to let go of my tail?

03:53.330 --> 03:54.560
I'm sorry.

03:54.560 --> 03:58.750
I was seeing if I could touch
 you in this dream, too.

03:58.750 --> 04:01.800
If you want to touch me too, you can.

04:01.800 --> 04:03.290
Like a real wolf.

04:03.620 --> 04:05.090
I'll pass!

04:07.700 --> 04:10.040
Is this the wolf's house?

04:10.040 --> 04:10.820
Yes.

04:11.160 --> 04:12.310
Let's go inside.

04:18.890 --> 04:20.990
I-It's really him!

04:21.360 --> 04:22.490
It is.

04:22.490 --> 04:26.450
B-But how do we defeat him? 
We don't have any weapons.

04:27.060 --> 04:29.160
Is that you, Little Red Riding Hood?

04:31.220 --> 04:34.600
What great big ears you have, Grandma.

04:34.600 --> 04:35.620
Alice!

04:36.080 --> 04:40.220
All the better to hear you with.

04:41.690 --> 04:45.190
What great big eyes you have, Grandma.

04:45.190 --> 04:46.800
Why are you looking at me?

04:47.110 --> 04:50.480
All the better to see you with.

04:52.810 --> 04:56.010
Your paws are so sexy, Your Grace.

04:56.010 --> 04:57.690
You just said "Your Grace"...

04:57.690 --> 05:01.380
All the better to grab you with, my dear.

05:01.380 --> 05:03.270
And he's not even listening!

05:03.270 --> 05:07.490
What a great big mouth you have, Grandma.

05:07.490 --> 05:09.460
All the better to eat—

05:09.460 --> 05:12.950
All the better to eat you with, Your Grace!

05:11.500 --> 05:12.950
Don't steal his line!

05:13.180 --> 05:16.910
You guys keep messing up the story!

05:16.910 --> 05:18.420
I'll eat you!

05:23.480 --> 05:26.800
Takashi, dinner time!

05:26.800 --> 05:30.050
Dinner time! Dinner time!

05:32.430 --> 05:34.560
Mommy! Mommy!

05:34.560 --> 05:36.420
He turned into a baby!

05:36.420 --> 05:39.440
Why did you exile me from the pack?

05:39.650 --> 05:42.120
I was so lonely!

05:42.120 --> 05:43.650
So lonely!

05:44.970 --> 05:47.360
So that's what happened, huh?

05:47.580 --> 05:49.530
Good work, you two.

05:49.530 --> 05:52.580
I'll take him in and raise him!

05:52.950 --> 05:56.600
So, about that wish...

05:56.600 --> 05:58.480
You didn't defeat him!

05:58.480 --> 06:01.480
Could you really hurt a 
defenseless child like this?

06:01.480 --> 06:03.000
Goo-goo!

06:03.910 --> 06:06.360
Wake up, loser!

06:19.750 --> 06:22.150
She looks so cute when she's asleep.

06:39.990 --> 06:41.210
<i>Walter?</i>

06:41.730 --> 06:43.710
Did you trip? Are you all right?

06:43.710 --> 06:46.260
Yes, I'm all right.

06:46.590 --> 06:48.420
Take care of yourself.

06:49.250 --> 06:54.140
Because if something happens to him, 
you'll become heir in his stead.

06:59.800 --> 07:01.300
<i>Ever since I was a kid,</i>

07:01.990 --> 07:05.690
<i>I've always known that everyone 
liked my brother more than me.</i>

07:07.320 --> 07:11.640
<i>They don't say it, but my mother 
and Viola both love him.</i>

07:12.870 --> 07:15.850
<i>They want him to become heir.</i>

07:16.830 --> 07:19.460
<i>My mother always looks out the window...</i>

07:21.160 --> 07:26.350
<i>Because she's waiting for him to 
break the curse and come home.</i>

07:36.920 --> 07:41.450
<i>The shady merchant in town said 
that if you wear this magical robe</i>

07:41.860 --> 07:45.320
<i>and touch a mirror on 
the night of a blood moon,</i>

07:45.320 --> 07:47.900
<i>you can go to the Sabbath, 
where witches gather.</i>

07:49.570 --> 07:53.300
<i>I need to find out the truth about 
the curse before the eldest does,</i>

07:53.850 --> 07:57.120
<i>and make them all realize 
I'm better than he is!</i>

07:59.080 --> 08:02.080
I'll beat him. I'll beat him no matter what.

08:02.080 --> 08:06.960
I'll beat him! I swear! I'll beat him!

08:08.880 --> 08:10.800
I'm not just his replacement!

08:13.140 --> 08:17.570
I'll prove that I'm worth something!

08:21.930 --> 08:23.940
You want to go back to the Sabbath?

08:24.730 --> 08:26.950
But why... are you dressed like that?

08:27.290 --> 08:32.400
The witches know my face, 
so I thought I'd wear a disguise.

08:32.970 --> 08:34.000
What do you think?

08:34.000 --> 08:38.120
All the cute things in this world 
put together aren't as cute as you!

08:38.450 --> 08:41.330
But Cuff and Zain aren't here...

08:41.900 --> 08:46.670
I want to see for myself if 
what Daleth said is true...

08:47.670 --> 08:50.070
I'm going to wake Sharon up from her slumber.

08:52.120 --> 08:57.430
We weren't able to finish our conversation, 
so I want to talk to her personally.

08:58.310 --> 08:59.950
I know it's dangerous.

08:59.950 --> 09:02.710
B-But how will you get to the Witches' World?

09:03.030 --> 09:05.640
Last time, Zain and Cuff took us,

09:05.970 --> 09:08.030
but it's not that easy this time.

09:08.880 --> 09:10.860
I'll use their magic.

09:14.350 --> 09:17.970
I borrowed the stone that Cuff had from Rob.

09:17.970 --> 09:20.280
The place you stored it was too sexy!

09:24.300 --> 09:27.980
Cuff liked it and kept 
it with her all the time.

09:27.980 --> 09:30.250
So it still has a little bit of magic.

09:31.480 --> 09:33.210
What will you do?

09:33.530 --> 09:35.720
I'm willing to go alone.

09:35.720 --> 09:37.650
O-Of course I'll go!

09:37.650 --> 09:40.050
I can't let you go by yourself!

09:40.900 --> 09:43.520
You're so brave, Your Grace.

09:44.480 --> 09:47.250
This is the present Zain gave us...

09:48.260 --> 09:49.230
Alice!

09:49.230 --> 09:51.690
W-Wait, Alice!

10:04.440 --> 10:06.130
<i>So this is the Witches' World?</i>

10:06.760 --> 10:08.710
<i>There are more people here than I thought.</i>

10:08.710 --> 10:10.190
<i>There'll be trouble if I'm caught.</i>

10:10.190 --> 10:11.670
No luck.

10:12.060 --> 10:15.420
Daleth refuses to come out of the church.

10:17.050 --> 10:19.090
No luck, huh?

10:19.310 --> 10:20.170
Yeah.

10:20.170 --> 10:22.440
Somebody saw her face, 
and now she's depressed.

10:22.440 --> 10:23.760
That's a problem.

10:23.760 --> 10:26.560
Can't start the Sabbath without the boss!

10:26.840 --> 10:28.850
<i>There's a more powerful witch here?</i>

10:29.320 --> 10:32.520
<i>Then I should try heading for that church!</i>

10:32.520 --> 10:36.390
That rich kid in the top hat is a jerk!

10:36.390 --> 10:38.490
<i>Him? The eldest?</i>

10:38.780 --> 10:42.450
I could never be friends 
with a wimp like him!

10:42.680 --> 10:45.670
<i>I know what you mean, miss!</i>

10:45.670 --> 10:47.440
<i>The enemy of an enemy is my friend!</i>

10:47.440 --> 10:50.480
<i>Someone who doesn't like the 
person I don't like is my friend!</i>

10:53.530 --> 10:54.670
Are you okay?

10:55.810 --> 10:57.440
Thanks, Alice...

10:59.370 --> 11:00.590
Walter!

11:01.340 --> 11:03.050
Who was that?

11:03.050 --> 11:04.550
Daleth?

11:04.550 --> 11:06.220
It's not Daleth!

11:09.890 --> 11:12.740
Alice, follow Walter!

11:13.900 --> 11:15.480
Hold it!

11:19.490 --> 11:21.520
Wait! Wait!

11:20.180 --> 11:21.320
Your Grace...

11:21.520 --> 11:22.990
Bye-bye!

11:30.610 --> 11:35.640
I don't know what happened to him,
 but why don't you head back?

11:36.110 --> 11:39.480
I was told to follow you.

11:40.330 --> 11:43.750
I get nervous when I'm alone with a girl.

11:43.750 --> 11:46.000
It would make me happy if you'd go away.

11:46.000 --> 11:47.300
I'm afraid I can't do that.

11:49.870 --> 11:51.590
Alice, was it?

11:52.010 --> 11:55.310
I can vaguely remember you being 
at our household when I was young.

11:55.980 --> 11:57.570
Are you okay with the way things are?

11:58.910 --> 12:01.720
Are you fine with being his servant?

12:01.720 --> 12:06.410
A young girl, stuck in that dark forest...
 I feel bad for you.

12:06.410 --> 12:10.370
No, I'm happy to be by His 
Grace's side each day.

12:10.910 --> 12:12.170
You are?

12:12.520 --> 12:14.330
He's not that special.

12:14.860 --> 12:19.040
You simply misunderstand His Grace.

12:19.040 --> 12:22.300
You're brothers, so you 
have similar personalities.

12:28.110 --> 12:31.070
Please don't lump me in with him...

12:31.070 --> 12:32.230
It really bugs me.

12:32.230 --> 12:35.230
I'm sorry. I didn't know.

12:35.630 --> 12:37.980
And especially don't use that word.

12:37.980 --> 12:41.190
Whenever somebody says I'm his 
little brother or the second son...

12:43.580 --> 12:45.370
It kills me!

12:48.670 --> 12:50.330
So this is the place?

12:50.330 --> 12:53.760
This is the church where the 
boss of the Witches' World is?

12:55.940 --> 12:58.310
<i>Is His Grace all right?</i>

12:58.730 --> 13:01.410
Trick or Treat?

13:01.410 --> 13:02.650
I'm sorry.

13:02.650 --> 13:04.750
I don't have any candy right now.

13:11.070 --> 13:12.330
Ow...

13:12.330 --> 13:14.430
Give that back to her.

13:14.760 --> 13:17.310
I just heard what you said before!

13:17.310 --> 13:20.090
It drives you nuts when people 
say you're the second son!

13:20.090 --> 13:22.410
Well, you'll be the second son forever, loser!

13:22.410 --> 13:23.830
That's not true.

13:23.830 --> 13:25.150
I can see it on your face!

13:25.150 --> 13:26.700
Bye, second son!

13:27.250 --> 13:27.860
Wait!

13:34.640 --> 13:36.540
What a strange place for a house.

13:37.140 --> 13:38.900
Can that pendant be repaired?

13:38.900 --> 13:39.740
Yes.

13:39.740 --> 13:42.800
The photo inside is what's important.

13:45.240 --> 13:46.500
Let's get it back.

13:46.500 --> 13:47.970
Wear this.

13:48.280 --> 13:51.990
A shady merchant in town told 
me that if you wear it,

13:51.990 --> 13:53.450
they won't realize you're human.

13:54.030 --> 13:56.190
I don't know how much 
it'll really help, but...

13:56.570 --> 13:58.440
You should wear it, Walter.

13:58.840 --> 14:00.120
It's fine.

14:00.120 --> 14:02.250
The witches back there already saw my face.

14:02.580 --> 14:05.450
Why are you being so kind?

14:05.450 --> 14:07.700
I'm protecting you because you're a girl.

14:09.160 --> 14:11.550
I'm not very experienced around women,

14:12.090 --> 14:16.060
but I was raised from birth 
to be polite to them.

14:16.380 --> 14:17.620
That's all.

14:18.460 --> 14:22.340
You're a kind man, just like His Grace.

14:26.310 --> 14:27.340
I'm sorry.

14:27.340 --> 14:28.760
Let's just go...

14:31.520 --> 14:33.260
You're finally here, second son!

14:33.260 --> 14:34.180
You little...

14:35.700 --> 14:37.270
Stupid second son!

14:37.270 --> 14:39.560
Come catch me if you don't like it!

14:41.860 --> 14:43.380
Smell ya later!

14:44.820 --> 14:47.240
I apologize for making you deal with this.

14:47.240 --> 14:50.320
No, he's gone too far.

14:50.320 --> 14:52.030
I'll set him straight after I catch him!

14:53.720 --> 14:55.240
I don't see him anywhere.

14:56.240 --> 14:58.460
This reminds me of when I was a child.

14:59.270 --> 15:00.870
My brother was terrible at hide-and-seek.

15:00.870 --> 15:02.960
I always found him right away.

15:03.770 --> 15:07.020
I'd hide somewhere cramped 
and not move at all.

15:07.650 --> 15:11.180
He wouldn't find me for hours. 
Sometimes, he'd forget me!

15:11.180 --> 15:13.900
And that was all my brother's fault!

15:15.410 --> 15:18.600
And so... hide-and-seek 
is something I excel at!

15:19.290 --> 15:22.350
He's hiding inside this closet...

15:22.600 --> 15:24.330
Or more precisely, behind it!

15:24.330 --> 15:27.070
Oh no! The stupid second son found me!

15:27.070 --> 15:28.430
Hold it!

15:28.430 --> 15:30.310
Hey, I'm over here!

15:30.650 --> 15:31.770
When did he get over there?

15:31.770 --> 15:33.420
Is there a secret passage?

15:33.420 --> 15:35.060
Well, I'll get him back!

15:35.060 --> 15:37.700
I'll get him back one vigintillion times!

15:37.700 --> 15:40.960
That's a very difficult word, you know.

15:41.080 --> 15:42.790
Up here!

15:42.920 --> 15:45.130
Get up here, second son!

15:45.250 --> 15:47.090
Come on and catch me!

15:47.230 --> 15:49.720
Man, being the second son must suck!

15:49.720 --> 15:51.190
This way!

15:51.190 --> 15:52.800
This way, second son!

15:52.800 --> 15:53.940
Second son! Second son!

15:53.940 --> 15:56.260
The unneeded one! The second son!

15:58.150 --> 15:59.500
Walter...

16:00.520 --> 16:03.690
<i>This stress is all the eldest's fault.</i>

16:04.540 --> 16:06.310
<i>I must focus...</i>

16:06.310 --> 16:07.920
Hey, what's wrong?

16:07.920 --> 16:09.650
Wimpy second son!

16:10.360 --> 16:12.860
Come catch me.

16:13.840 --> 16:15.680
I'm done chasing you.

16:17.370 --> 16:19.030
You've given up already?

16:19.030 --> 16:20.700
Loser!

16:20.700 --> 16:22.820
There are two of you, aren't there?

16:24.060 --> 16:26.500
You're twins who look the exactly same.

16:27.200 --> 16:28.880
The older brother is the 
one who took the pendant.

16:28.880 --> 16:29.460
Gulp...

16:30.070 --> 16:33.390
And you look like you're wearing 
hand-me-downs, so you're the younger.

16:33.390 --> 16:37.760
And... you never made fun of me 
for being a second son, did you?

16:40.920 --> 16:42.680
I found the older brother.

16:42.680 --> 16:44.280
What are you doing?

16:44.280 --> 16:46.530
They caught me because of you!

16:46.530 --> 16:48.070
I-I'm sorry.

16:48.070 --> 16:49.490
Are you really going to take that?

16:50.440 --> 16:54.360
You don't have to do everything your older 
brother says just because you're younger.

16:54.890 --> 16:56.510
You can get him back.

16:57.170 --> 16:59.080
That's what it means to be brothers.

17:00.810 --> 17:03.290
Now give back the pendant, please.

17:03.290 --> 17:04.750
No!

17:06.090 --> 17:07.100
Here.

17:07.100 --> 17:08.710
Thank you.

17:08.710 --> 17:10.540
What do you think you're doing, loser?

17:10.540 --> 17:12.420
Shut up! Stop bossing me around!

17:13.650 --> 17:19.140
<i>Perhaps you're much nicer 
than I thought, Walter.</i>

17:20.800 --> 17:24.060
You really are just like His Grace.

17:28.260 --> 17:30.000
You okay, second son?

17:30.000 --> 17:31.780
Get a hold of yourself!

17:40.260 --> 17:41.450
I just can't do it.

17:42.990 --> 17:44.950
I can't get over it...

17:44.950 --> 17:50.760
Daleth, your face looks just like mine,
 so it's hard to tell us apart.

17:51.160 --> 17:53.420
Would it be all right if I changed that?

18:01.690 --> 18:05.460
You're really climbing up there?

18:05.460 --> 18:09.100
Yes, it will be safer than 
going in through the front.

18:09.890 --> 18:14.570
If I can get inside, I'll unlock 
the door. So wait for me!

18:14.570 --> 18:16.320
<i>He's incredibly bold.</i>

18:19.130 --> 18:23.790
Sister... how could you be so 
innocent about hurting someone?

18:24.660 --> 18:30.460
Why did you die and leave 
me in charge of everything?

18:31.800 --> 18:33.760
I hate you, Sister!

18:34.310 --> 18:39.310
You're selfish, and arrogant, and 
you don't understand me at all!

18:42.430 --> 18:44.510
You ruined my life!

18:45.370 --> 18:49.650
I'll never be able to forgive you!

18:49.650 --> 18:52.020
I know exactly how you feel!

18:52.020 --> 18:52.940
Who's there?

18:52.940 --> 18:55.280
I know exactly how you feel!

18:55.280 --> 18:56.900
You just said the same thing twice!

18:57.610 --> 19:00.280
What are you doing in my church?

19:03.700 --> 19:06.700
You're that young man's little brother?

19:07.130 --> 19:08.490
I'm Walter...

19:08.930 --> 19:11.420
Sorry, I heard what you said.

19:11.920 --> 19:14.800
I know it's strange to feel 
sympathy for a witch.

19:15.380 --> 19:17.570
But I hate my brother too!

19:17.570 --> 19:20.820
My whole life was decided from 
the start because of him!

19:20.820 --> 19:25.890
He's selfish! Arrogant!
He doesn't understand me at all!

19:26.950 --> 19:28.740
You're just like me!

19:29.170 --> 19:30.790
What are you talking about?

19:30.790 --> 19:32.850
And why did you even come here?

19:33.610 --> 19:35.990
To learn about my brother's curse.

19:35.990 --> 19:38.570
I'd planned to stay in the shadows but...

19:39.740 --> 19:42.280
I couldn't just ignore a crying lady.

19:43.770 --> 19:46.740
I'm not a lady! We're not the same!

19:47.280 --> 19:50.070
My face is ugly and scarred!

19:50.070 --> 19:52.410
A handsome man like you 
could never understand!

19:52.410 --> 19:53.960
No, we're the same!

19:54.490 --> 19:58.610
No matter what I look like, 
right now I'm just his replacement.

19:59.060 --> 20:01.950
My scars are there. You just can't see them.

20:04.790 --> 20:05.890
You don't need to hide your face.

20:07.730 --> 20:08.850
Look at me.

20:09.870 --> 20:11.810
You're beautiful.

20:12.670 --> 20:14.520
You should be more confident in yourself.

20:17.610 --> 20:20.690
Daleth! We caught two rats snooping around!

20:21.190 --> 20:25.660
We all had an awful time tying 
him up without touching him.

20:27.370 --> 20:30.080
Sorry! I know you don't like 
people seeing your face!

20:32.280 --> 20:35.790
How do you deal with your scars?

20:37.300 --> 20:38.600
I accept them.

20:40.170 --> 20:43.390
I can't change the fact that 
I'm just a replacement for him.

20:43.390 --> 20:44.320
But...

20:44.900 --> 20:48.920
I can work to show I'm 
more valuable than he is.

20:51.540 --> 20:54.230
Nothing will ever change if you 
don't look toward the future.

20:56.110 --> 20:57.230
That's right.

20:58.400 --> 21:00.740
It's time for me to get over this.

21:37.170 --> 21:40.040
I'm sorry for being depressed for so long.

21:40.730 --> 21:43.180
From now on, I'll act more like this.

21:43.600 --> 21:44.690
Thanks, everyone.

21:48.970 --> 21:52.120
You're beautiful, Miss Daleth!

21:52.120 --> 21:54.410
You're pretty!

23:34.970 --> 23:40.250
The Duke of Death and His Maid
The Duke, Alice, and the Kissing Window

23:35.470 --> 23:39.930
"The Duke, Alice, and the Kissing Window."
